<title>FRANCE: Schiphol leads April cargo growth. London 4mo..</title>
<headline>Schiphol leads April cargo growth. London 4mo..</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amsterdam's Schiphol airport recorded the highest percentage gain in cargo traffic in April 1997 compared to April 1996 levels, amongst the EU's top cargo-handling airports, figures issued by the Paris airports authority (ADP) show.</p>
<p>The London airports recorded the highest growth for January-April 1997. The ADP details in tonnes included:</p>
<p>    Airport	 April     Percent vs</p>
<p>				   April 1996</p>
<p>    London*	123,276     up  7.0</p>
<p>    Frankfurt    110,665     up  1.7</p>
<p>    Amsterdam     95,376     up  8.0</p>
<p>    Paris**	 92,592     up  2.2</p>
<p>    Airport     Jan-April   Percent vs</p>
<p>				   Jan-April 1996</p>
<p>    London*	490,379     up  7.8</p>
<p>    Frankfurt    440,113     up  3.9</p>
<p>    Amsterdam    375,833     up  4.9</p>
<p>    Paris**	365,702     up  2.5</p>
<p>*  includes Heathrow, Gatwick and Stansted ** includes Charles de Gaulle and Orly - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
